Item 02 is done. The campaign ran in full, the audit is clean, and the report, PROGRESS.md and iterations.md are written. Nothing was committed, and nothing touched `solutions/`.

**What ran.** The grid §9 chose, with no shortfall: 7 sizes from n = 10 to 40, m ∈ {n, 2n}, fixed d from 2 to 10 and Bernoulli p from 0.025 to 0.5. That is 252 cells at 150 instances each, 37,800 in total. The 8,000 pilot rows were reused with the same seeds and 29,800 new instances ran in 382 s of wall clock on 16 workers while recertify kept its 9 cores.

| quantity | value |
|---|---|
| total compute | 2.16 core-hours (508 s wall incl. pilot) |
| witnesses re-simulating | 37,800 of 37,800 |
| `optimum − 1` refuted, both configs | 37,794 (+6 with optimum 1) |
| `sat` or deadline | 0 |
| manifest digests regenerated | 37,800 of 37,800 |
| complete graphs | 6,511 (17.2%), all optimum n |
| decomposable | 7,101 (18.8%), kept |
| isomorphic repeats within cells | 10,479 (27.7%) |
| cells with <10% complete and <50% decomposable | 145 of 252, 20,652 classes |
| artifact size | 40.6 MB |

**Report §10** in `reports/ml_nature.md` holds the audit, compute breakdown, the by-size table, dedupe per n, and twelve per-cell density × n matrices for classes per instance, complete share and decomposable share. It stays descriptive as the item requires. One method note is worth flagging: seconds per instance at n = 40 doubled between the pilot and the campaign on identical instances, while node counts reproduced exactly on 400 re-refuted samples, which supports the plan's rule of nodes over seconds.

**Code and tests.** `learning/ensemble.py` gained the `--item02` flag and three table functions. Two tests were added and the full suite passed with 784 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed in 76 s.

**Next** is item 03, the phase-transition question, reading node counts from the campaign CSV with `col_mean` as the density axis.

